{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["Maskit — from שכה, like מרבית from רבה. And I find no parallel for it except its counterpart עברו משכיות לבב — the language of 'reflections of the heart'; so too here, a stone that has images and figures on it to gaze upon."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {0 "The prooftext cited elliptically is from Ezekiel 8:12; Rashbam's leap from שכה to 'reflections' follows his midrashic source which reads משכיות as derived from a root meaning to see/reflect."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:26.455717413Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}